[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: KM271-WiFi High-Level Software Requirements
UID: KM271-SW
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
High-level requirements on the application firmware of the KM271-WiFi.
They are deliberately independent of a specific implementation: they
apply to every firmware that targets the board, currently
the78mole/ESPhome-KM271-WiFi (ESPHome with the km271_wifi component) and
dewenni/ESP_Buderus_KM271 (Arduino/PlatformIO with WebUI and MQTT).
How a firmware meets a requirement (YAML option, WebUI setting, compile
option) is left to the implementation. COMPLIANCE is therefore not filled
in here; it belongs to the verification of each firmware.

The requirements trace to the system requirements (KM271-SYS-xxx) and to
the application firmware block and interfaces of the system architecture.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Logamatic communication

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-001
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: KM271 link protocol
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall communicate with the Logamatic over the KM271 serial
interface at 2400 Bd, 8N1, using the 3964R link protocol including
acknowledge, retry and timeout handling.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-101

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-002
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Serial port configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall use GPIO17 as TX and GPIO18 as RX for the KM271 line on the
v2.0 board. The pins should be configurable to support other boards.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-101

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-003
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Continuous data reception
STATEMENT: >>>
After start-up and after any loss of communication the firmware shall switch
the Logamatic into log mode so that it reports all values and their changes
continuously.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-004
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Decoding of values
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall decode at least the values of heating circuit 1 and 2, hot
water, boiler and burner, outdoor temperature, operating modes and error/alarm
messages into physical units and states.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-005
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Writing parameters
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall offer write access to the parameters supported by the KM271
interface (e.g. operating mode and set points of the heating circuits, hot
water mode and temperature) and shall reject values outside the range the
Logamatic accepts.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-006
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Communication supervision
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall detect a missing or faulty KM271 communication within 60 s,
report it as a status value and retry the connection automatically.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-023
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Network

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-010
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: WiFi station mode
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall connect to a configured WiFi network as station and
reconnect automatically after a loss of connection.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-107

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-011
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Setup access point
STATEMENT: >>>
If no network is configured or the configured network is unreachable, the
firmware shall open an access point with a configuration page (captive portal)
for entering the WiFi credentials.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-033
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-012
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: WiFi power saving
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall keep the WiFi modem power save mode enabled by default.
Disabling it shall be an explicit user option with a warning about the higher
supply load.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Disabling modem sleep raises the average current by about 60-80 mA and caused
brown-outs with weak Logamatic supplies (dewenni v6.0.0).
<<<
SOURCE: brownout-v6-2026-11-20 analysis
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-012
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-013
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Wired Ethernet
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall support the W5500 Ethernet extension on the SPI interface
of J7 as alternative or in addition to WiFi.
<<<
COMMENT: Details in the software requirements of the extension (ETH-SW-xxx).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-005
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-103

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-014
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Network time
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware should synchronise its clock via NTP for time stamps and time
based functions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Integration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-020
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Home automation interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall publish all decoded values and accept commands for all
writable parameters through at least one of: MQTT, ESPHome native API.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-006
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-021
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Home Assistant discovery
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall make its entities discoverable by Home Assistant without
manual entity configuration.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-006
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-022
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Local web interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware should provide a local web interface showing the current values
and the device status.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-006
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Local inputs and outputs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-030
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: OneWire temperature sensors
STATEMENT: The firmware should read DS18B20 compatible OneWire sensors on GPIO15.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-021
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-104

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-031
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Analog sensor inputs
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware should read the analog inputs of J6 (GPIO6/7/8) and offer a
conversion to temperature for NTC sensors.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-021
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-104

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-032
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Oil meter
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware should count pulses of an oil meter on the oil meter input with
configurable debounce time and pulses per litre, and store the counter
persistently.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-021
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-033
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Supply voltage monitor
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall measure the +5V rail on GPIO4 and publish it with a user
calibration factor.
<<<
RATIONALE: Allows users to diagnose weak Logamatic supplies.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-034
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Status LEDs
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall drive the LEDs as: GPIO21 network connected, GPIO38
heartbeat, GPIO39 Logamatic communication active, GPIO40 error.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-023
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-035
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Could
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: User buttons
STATEMENT: The firmware may assign functions to the user buttons on GPIO41/42.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-024
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Installation and updates

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-040
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Initial flashing over USB
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be provided as a complete image that can be flashed over
the native USB of the ESP32-S3 and over the CP2102N path, e.g. with a browser
based installer.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-031
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-041
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Constraint
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Native USB must stay usable
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall not reconfigure GPIO19/GPIO20 or disable the USB peripheral
in a way that prevents re-flashing over the native USB.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-203

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-042
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Over-the-air update
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall support updates over the network. An update shall only be
installed if it was built for the chip of the device (ESP32-S3 vs. ESP32).
<<<
RATIONALE: A generic OTA download could pick an ESP32 image for an S3 board.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-032
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-200

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-043
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Board preset
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware should offer a preset or default configuration for the KM271-WiFi
v2.0 pin assignment.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Robustness and security

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-050
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Persistent configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The configuration shall survive power cycles and firmware updates and should
be exportable and restorable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-051
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Watchdog and recovery
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall recover from hangs by a watchdog reset and shall resume
operation after a power failure without user interaction.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-052
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Diagnostics
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall provide log output over USB (serial) and should provide a
network log for diagnosis.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-102

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-053
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Security
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Access protection
STATEMENT: >>>
Write access to heating parameters, configuration and OTA updates shall be
protectable by a password set by the user.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-032
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Firmware alternatives

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SW-060
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Constraint
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: ESP32-S3 support in all firmwares
STATEMENT: >>>
Each supported firmware project shall provide an ESP32-S3 build for the v2.0
board.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
dewenni v6.0.x builds for ESP32-S3 without code changes but has no S3 release;
ESPHome-KM271-WiFi has no S3 configuration yet.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-200

[[/SECTION]]
